################################################################################
INSTALLING AOCL BINARY PACKAGES
################################################################################

1. Use the command tar -xvf <aocl-linux-<compiler>-5.0.0.tar.gz> to untar the 
   package.

2. The installer file install.sh is available in aocl-linux-<compiler>-5.0.0.

3. Run ./install.sh to install the AOCL package (all libraries) to the default 
   INSTALL_PATH: /home/<username>/aocl/5.0.0/<compiler>, where the compiler 
   value is aocc or gcc.

4. To install the AOCL package in a custom location, use the installer with 
   the option: -t <CUSTOM_PATH>.
   For example, ./install.sh -t /home/<username>.

5. The master installer can also be used to install individual library out of 
   the master package.
    – To install a specific library, use the option -l followed by the 
      library name.
      For example, ./install.sh -l blis
      The library names that have been used are fftw, libm, crypto, libmem, 
      blis, libflame, scalapack, rng, secrng, sparse and utils.
    – You can also install the individual library in a path of your choice.
      For example, ./install.sh -t /home/amd -l blis

6. Use -h option for "USAGE" help to be printed with all the supported options.

7. To change the default library path to ILP64 / LP64, copy the script 
   set_aocl_interface_symlink.sh to the <AOCL INSTALL PATH> and run
    – cd <AOCL INSTALL PATH>
    – bash set_aocl_interface_symlink.sh <ilp64/lp64>

8. Please untar the package 
   aocl-libmem-avx512-linux-<compiler name>-<release-version>.tar.gz manually 
   to use libmem AVX512 binaries to support Zen4 architecture.

Refer to the AOCL User Guide in "Chapter 3 - Installing AOCL" for detailed steps.
